MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Hypnotic Eye feels like a natural next choice because Tom Petty connects directly with my recent Benmont Tench listening, and I want more of that rock sound today.",
    "The Gregg Allman tribute appeals through bluesy Southern rock, while the blues guitar in Tour De Force connects with my Clapton and Hendrix listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "World Wide Rebel Songs misses my current mood because politically focused folk rock is less appealing to me than blues and classic rock.",
    "Live At Radio City Music Hall and Very Best Of leave me unsure whose music I would hear; a live recording or compilation alone gives me no reason to choose it."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in roots-oriented music seems to have been stretched too broadly: country and folk connections do not make an album as compelling as Petty or Allman today.",
    "An established rock artist can fit my taste without being an immediate choice; High Hopes interests me, but the connection to my latest listening makes Hypnotic Eye stronger."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent Benmont Tench listening makes the specific connection to Tom Petty especially meaningful right now.",
    "I rarely choose several albums at once. Being interested in a blues live set or roots-rock album does not mean I would act on it when Petty and Allman already stand out."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations capture my blues and roots-rock interests, but some broad musical connections are weaker than the specific Petty connection and Allman's Southern rock appeal today."
}
